WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.490
Same business. Same inventory request.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.160
Under stress, the lender offers
less than half.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.450
Which advance pays off first?

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.710
I ran this study in DBeaver,
one SQL program at a time.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.300
First, I checked the prior stage
had passed and the right policy was loaded.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.430
If we fund this advance,
what could it contribute?

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.560
The calculation accounts for costs,
expected losses,

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.810
and the cost of putting capital at risk.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.340
A separate program checked
the saved results.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.200
If the amounts disagreed, I could trace
the failed check back to the figures.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.960
I tested what should go wrong, too.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.710
Disabling the policy had to stop
the calculation.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.980
The next stage received the results
and the evidence behind them.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.600
Tableau pairs the same 750 applications.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.790
103 received financing in Baseline

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.080
and 27 under stress.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.320
Two full approvals became counteroffers.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.300
Merchant 98 was one.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.270
In Power BI, Baseline funded
the full $5,200.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.610
10.9% of eligible sales
went toward repayment.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:22.370
Under stress, the lender offered $2,500.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.650
The same share of daily sales
now went toward a smaller balance.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.270
Follow the two balances.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.330
The smaller advance paid off on day 85.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.220
On day 120, the larger advance still had

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.900
over $1,700 outstanding.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:43.000
Did this merchant do better under stress?

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.670
Both the sales path and the offer changed.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.620
That matters when comparing repayment.

